$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General experimental procedure for the preparation of oxazole or
isoxazole-3-carboxylic acid coupled amino acids (1-9): To a solution of
5-methylisoxazole-3-carboxylic acid (0.5 g, 3.94 mmol)) in
dichloromethane (DCM) (16 ml, 0.25 M) was added triethylamine (TEA) (1.13
ml, 7.88 mmol), EDC.HCl (0.91 g, 4.73 mmol) and HOBT (0.53 g, 3.94 mmol)
at 0 oC. After stirring the reaction mixture for 5 min, the amino acid
methyl ester hydrochloride (0.72 g, 4.73 mmol) was added. Then the
reaction mixture was bringing to room temperature and stir for overnight.
Water was added and the mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate. The
combined organic layers were washed with brine and dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was
purified by silica gel flash column chromatography to afford the desired
product. (S)-Methyl 2-(5-methylisoxazole-3-carboxamido) butanoate (1):
According to the general experimental procedure, compound 1 was prepared
from methyl ester of (L) 2-aminobutyric acid (H-Abu-OMe.HCl). A colorless
solid in 0.69 g (78% yield). R f = 0.3 in hexane/ethyl acetate = 3/1. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.23 (d, J = 6.9, 1H), 6.41 (s, 1H), 4.73-4.68
(m, 1H), 3.76 (s, 3H), 2.46 (s, 3H), 2.02-1.95 (m, 1H), 1.85-1.78 (m,
1H), 0.98 (dt, J = 7.4, 1.0 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 172.0,
171.3, 158.8, 158.3, 101.4, 77.3, 77.0, 76.7, 53.3, 52.4, 25.6, 12.3,
9.6. HRMS: calculated for C10H15N2O4 [M+H+]: 227.1037; found: 227.1032.
